# Worker (Cloudflare / Hono)

## Role

Optional edge API in `worker/` — proxies or replaces Python API in production per `docs/p0-cloudflare-stack.md`. Local dev often hits Python on `:8787` via `web/lib/api.ts`.

## Layout

```text
worker/src/index.ts   # Hono routes (health, sessions stub)
worker/wrangler.toml  # name, compatibility_date, vars
```

## Conventions

- TypeScript strict; `npm run typecheck` in CI.
- Wrangler requires **Node ≥ 22** (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
- Keep request/response shapes aligned with `server/src/api/schemas.py` when implementing real proxy logic.
- Secrets/bindings (D1, R2, Container) belong in wrangler + dashboard — not committed.

## Verification

```bash
cd worker && npm ci && npm run typecheck && npx wrangler deploy --dry-run
```

Do not add heavy frameworks; match existing Hono minimal style.
